{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CeRPD3cQ7edpYoaGNiT72","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\"task_id\":\"aviation_safety-029\",\"optimization_analysis\":\"Three changes reduce LM cost: (1) The flight_phase predicate (CONTAINS 'Approach' OR 'Landing') is a structured field in incidents.csv — moving it into the initial SCAN_TABLE FILTER eliminates non-approach/landing incidents before any document scanning occurs. (2) Both structured side-tables (environment_attributes and events) are joined before SCAN_DOCS/SEM_FILTER rather than after, so only incidents that already satisfy the flight_conditions and result-label constraints are fetched as documents and sent to the LM — this can cut the document set substantially. (3) The two sequential SEM_FILTERs (positive cause check then negative cause exclusion) are merged into one, halving the number of LM calls per surviving document. Semantics are unchanged: the combined prompt enforces both the inclusion and exclusion criteria simultaneously.\",\"optimized_semantic_plan\":[{\"type\":\"operator_dag\",\"program\":\"approach_incidents := (\\n  SCAN_TABLE(NASA_ASRS, incidents.csv, [incident_id, text_file, local_time_of_day, flight_phase])\\n  -> FILTER(local_time_of_day = '1201-1800' AND (flight_phase CONTAINS 'Approach' OR flight_phase CONTAINS 'Landing'))\\n)\\nenvironment_records := (\\n  SCAN_TABLE(NASA_ASRS, environment_attributes.csv, [incident_id, attribute, value])\\n  -> FILTER(attribute = 'flight_conditions' AND value IN ('IMC','Marginal','Mixed'))\\n)\\nresult_events := (\\n  SCAN_TABLE(NASA_ASRS, events.csv, [incident_id, event_type, label])\\n  -> FILTER(event_type = 'result' AND label IN ('Flight Crew Executed Go Around / Missed Approach','Air Traffic Control Issued New Clearance'))\\n)\\nstructured_candidates := JOIN(left=approach_incidents, right=environment_records, join_type=inner, condition=approach_incidents.incident_id = environment_records.incident_id)\\nstructured_candidates_with_events := JOIN(left=structured_candidates, right=result_events, join_type=inner, condition=structured_candidates.incident_id = result_events.incident_id)\\nsemantic_candidates := (\\n  structured_candidates_with_events\\n  -> SCAN_DOCS(NASA_ASRS, selector=structured_candidates_with_events.text_file, [incident_id, text])\\n  -> SEM_FILTER(\\\"Keep reports where weather or visibility explicitly caused the go-around, missed approach, or new clearance. Exclude reports where traffic spacing, runway occupancy, or aircraft equipment was the primary cause of that outcome.\\\", {text})\\n)\\nsemantic_candidates\\n-> GROUP_BY([flight_conditions:value, recorded_result=CASE label WHEN 'Flight Crew Executed Go Around / Missed Approach' THEN 'go_around_or_missed_approach' ELSE 'new_clearance' END], {incident_count:COUNT_DISTINCT(incident_id)})\"}]}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7704,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7704,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b31b16d5-123a-4b99-8a6a-7ec263ab890d","uuid":"0d8f7d40-3a29-4e04-9e80-fe2d534e6c1d"}
